# Nootbuk — Project Rules

## What This Is
Nootbuk is a musician's idea capture and song documentation tool. Desktop-first client-side web app. No backend at MVP. All data in IndexedDB. Read AGENTS.md for the phased build plan.

## Stack (pinned versions — do not upgrade without discussion)
- React 19.x (19.2.x latest patches)
- Vite 8.x with @tailwindcss/vite plugin
- TypeScript 5.x, strict mode
- Tailwind CSS v4 (CSS-first config via @theme, NOT tailwind.config.ts)
- shadcn/ui (new-york style, OKLCH colors, npx shadcn@latest)
- Dexie.js 4.4.x (IndexedDB wrapper)
- Tone.js 15.x (synth engine)
- smplr (soundfont playback — NOT soundfont-player, which is archived)
- @spotify/basic-pitch (audio-to-MIDI, client-side TF.js)
- @tonejs/midi (MIDI file I/O)
- @dnd-kit (drag and drop — NOT react-beautiful-dnd)
- Zustand or Jotai for UI state (NOT Redux). Data lives in Dexie, not state management.
- NO rich text editors. No Tiptap, no BlockNote, no ProseMirror. Plain textarea everywhere.

## Critical Constraints
- NO backend, NO server, NO API calls, NO auth. Everything runs client-side.
- NO Next.js, NO SSR. This is a Vite SPA.
- NO Electron/Tauri. Runs in a browser tab.
- Feature-detect Web MIDI API (navigator.requestMIDIAccess) — not available in Safari/iOS.
- Feature-detect File System Access API (window.showSaveFilePicker) — not available in Firefox/Safari. Use browser-fs-access library for fallback.
- Audio recording via AudioWorklet capturing PCM, encode to WAV manually. Do NOT rely on MediaRecorder for WAV output (browsers output webm/opus or mp4/aac, not wav).
- All IDs are UUIDs via crypto.randomUUID()
- All timestamps are ISO 8601 strings
- Data schema must map cleanly to Postgres later — explicit foreign keys, no nested objects for relational data.

## File Structure
```
/nootbuk/
  /public/
    /soundfonts/          # GM soundfont files loaded by smplr
  /src/
    /app/                 # App shell, routing, layout
    /components/
      /ui/                # shadcn/ui components (copy-pasted, not imported from a package)
      /capture/           # Audio recorder, MIDI recorder, note picker, capture modal
      /song/              # Song workspace, section list, idea cards
      /album/             # Album view
      /pool/              # Idea pool browser
      /ideas/             # Ideas list page
      /instruments/       # Instrument management
      /player/            # Playback controls, synth patch selector
      /export/            # Export dialog and logic
      /shared/            # Shared components (layout, nav, etc.)
    /hooks/
      useMidi.ts          # Web MIDI API connection and recording
      useAudioRecorder.ts # AudioWorklet-based PCM capture + WAV encoding
      useSynth.ts         # Tone.js + smplr initialization and playback
      useAudioToMidi.ts   # @spotify/basic-pitch wrapper
      useExport.ts        # Export logic (File System Access + JSZip fallback)
      useDb.ts            # Dexie CRUD operations
    /lib/
      db.ts               # Dexie database definition and schema
      midi.ts             # MIDI file read/write utilities (@tonejs/midi)
      notes.ts            # Note name/number conversion utilities
      export.ts           # Folder structure builder, zip creation
      audio.ts            # WAV encoding, audio utilities
    /stores/              # Zustand/Jotai stores for UI-only state
    /types/               # TypeScript interfaces (Idea, Song, Album, etc.)
  /tests/
```

## Coding Conventions
- Functional components only, no class components.
- Use React 19 patterns: ref as prop (not forwardRef), use() hook where appropriate.
- Named exports for components. Default export only for pages/routes.
- Colocate component-specific types in the component file. Shared types in /types/.
- Error boundaries around audio/MIDI operations — these APIs can fail on permission denial or device disconnect.
- Every Dexie operation should be in a try/catch — IndexedDB can throw on quota, corruption, or private browsing.
- Console.warn (not silent failure) when Web MIDI or File System Access is unavailable.

## Do NOT
- Do not install tailwind config files (tailwind.config.ts/js). Tailwind v4 uses CSS-first @theme.
- Do not use @tailwind directives. Use @import "tailwindcss" in CSS.
- Do not use forwardRef — React 19 passes ref as a regular prop.
- Do not store UI state in Dexie. Dexie is for persistent data only.
- Do not hardcode pixel widths for layout. Use responsive primitives even though MVP targets desktop.
- Do not add any cloud/server dependencies.
- Do not use localStorage or sessionStorage for app data — IndexedDB via Dexie only.
